60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Ledger Bridge is pure software. No appraisals, no physical inventory. It fits my need for a clean quarter-end.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Ledger Bridge is the back-office tooling. It is the quiet kind that kept its customers. I am voting for it.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,Ledger Bridge does not tie up cash in stock. It is a service. My credit line will treat it as a viable asset.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mio,,Ledger Bridge is software. I can find the engineers and support staff. I do not need to hunt for field crews.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Ledger Bridge runs inside the bank's cycle. No hardware, no supply chain. The first customer can switch on immediately.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, yes, and it is verifiable. The data comes from the banks, not just their own dashboard.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, exactly. The retention was high because it solved a real, boring problem. It is not a fad.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Toshio, I agree. It is the safest path for our liquidity. We can borrow against the subscription contracts if we need to.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Minako, and I can actually staff it. The recruiters have placed software teams before. I am not stuck.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, yes. The only risk is the bank's own security review, but that is a known, manageable delay.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,I am voting for Ledger Bridge. It is the only one that does not add complexity to our reporting.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I am voting for Ledger Bridge. It is the model that actually kept its customers and paid the returns.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,I am voting for Ledger Bridge. It protects our borrowing power and keeps our reserves intact for the future.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mio,,I am voting for Ledger Bridge. It is the only one I can actually staff without losing a week to recruitment.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I am voting for Ledger Bridge. It has no external blockers. The money goes in, and the first customer switches on.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is unanimous. We are choosing the clean, verifiable, and staffable model.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I am satisfied. We are choosing the truth over the story.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,I am confident. We are choosing the model that keeps our fund healthy.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Mio,,I am happy. We are choosing the model that I can actually help build.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I am at peace. We are choosing the model where the road is clear.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
